Third-party components
======================

The executable bca-alert-client and the Docker image built by the
Dockerfile combine this client with the following components.

Statically linked into bca-alert-client:

  pl_mqtt v0.1.0             GPL-3.0-or-later
    https://github.com/CodiePP/pl_mqtt/tree/v0.1.0
  pl_kafka v0.1.0            GPL-3.0-or-later
    https://github.com/CodiePP/pl_kafka/tree/v0.1.0
  prolog-utilities v0.1.0    GPL-3.0-or-later
    (pl_toolbox/src/json.pl)
    https://github.com/CodiePP/prolog-utilities/tree/v0.1.0
  GNU Prolog 1.5.0 runtime   LGPL-3.0-or-later OR GPL-2.0-or-later
    https://www.gprolog.org/

Dynamically linked, from Debian trixie packages:

  libmosquitto1 2.0.21       EPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause (Eclipse Distribution License 1.0)
  librdkafka1 2.8.0          BSD-2-Clause
  OpenSSL 3, glibc, libcurl, cyrus-sasl and further libraries that
  librdkafka depends on, each under its own license.

Also in the Docker image:

  tini 0.19.0                MIT
  ca-certificates            MPL-2.0 (certificate data), GPL-2.0-or-later
  Debian trixie base image   various

Because the GPL-3.0-or-later components are linked into the executable,
the executable and the Docker image as a whole are distributed under the
terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later. The
Apache-2.0 licensed client source is compatible with this. The
corresponding source of the GPL components is at the URLs above.

The Docker image contains the license texts in /usr/share/doc/bca-alert-client/
and, for the Debian packages, in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
